"Goats tend to unhear honks\nThey unsee the car incoming\nIt then hit them and hurts\nThe goat who was there standing\n\nThey tend to ignore companions\nBut they want to be with them\nThey strangle over and over\nGiving the warmth and recieving the same\n\nHowever they are born foolish\nCan't tell who's a butcher\nAnd then they complain that\nThe cruel world want them to perish\n\nYes the world is bad\nAnd it always will\nBut the goat should be aware enough\nTo see the valley and the hill\n\nYes they are innocent\nIn some ways very cunning\nTheir intentions are both good and evil\nDepending on the person they start strangling\n\nStrangling is not bad\nBut if done at wrong time and place\nIt's dangerous for the goat\nAnd the companion itself\n\nYes they want attention\nThey won't always get it\nYes they wish to be loved\nThey will but not if they won't edit"